      "tabname": "Details",
      "class": "DepictionStackView",
      "views": [
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "**RootRun** makes the apps you choose launch as **root** (uid 0) instead of the usual sandboxed user. It's the jailbreak equivalent of running something with **sudo** — useful for apps that need full filesystem access.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "How to use"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "1. Open **Settings → RootRun**.\n2. Tap **Apps** and switch on each app you want to run as root.\n3. Force-quit that app, then open it again — it now runs as root.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Good to know"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "- Only apps on this device are affected. Nothing leaves the phone.\n- Running as root removes the app's sandbox, so only switch on apps you trust.\n- System apps are left out of the list on purpose.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
